## 3. How `checkout_transaction`/`void_transaction` currently build and call `private.post_journal()`

The **current/latest** version is in `supabase/migrations/20260710140000_ppn_liability.sql` (this is the 3rd and final redefinition after `20260708300100_checkout_void_journal_posting.sql` → `20260709120000_fix_zero_total_hpp_posting.sql` → `20260710140000_ppn_liability.sql`; confirmed no later migration touches `checkout_transaction`/`void_transaction`/`seed_default_accounts` via grep except `20260710150000_fixed_assets_depreciation.sql` which only re-touches `seed_default_accounts`, quoted in §4).

**checkout_transaction journal-posting block** (lines 286–315 of `20260710140000_ppn_liability.sql`):

```sql
  -- Auto-post the sale to the journal: Kas & Bank debited for the full total,
  -- but only (subtotal + service) — the business's actual earnings — is
  -- credited to Pendapatan Penjualan. PPN collected from the customer is
  -- credited to PPN Keluaran (a liability) instead, since it's held on
  -- behalf of the tax office, not revenue. Plus HPP / Persediaan
  -- independently whenever this sale had recipe-based cost data, even on a
  -- 100%-discount sale where v_total is 0 but stock was still consumed.
  v_journal_lines := '[]'::jsonb;
  if v_total > 0 then
    v_journal_lines := v_journal_lines || jsonb_build_array(
      jsonb_build_object('account_code', '1-001', 'debit', v_total, 'credit', 0),
      jsonb_build_object('account_code', '4-001', 'debit', 0, 'credit', v_subtotal + v_service)
    );
    if v_tax > 0 then
      v_journal_lines := v_journal_lines || jsonb_build_array(
        jsonb_build_object('account_code', '2-200', 'debit', 0, 'credit', v_tax)
      );
    end if;
  end if;
  if v_total_cost > 0 then
    v_journal_lines := v_journal_lines || jsonb_build_array(
      jsonb_build_object('account_code', '5-001', 'debit', v_total_cost, 'credit', 0),
      jsonb_build_object('account_code', '1-200', 'debit', 0, 'credit', v_total_cost)
    );
  end if;
  if jsonb_array_length(v_journal_lines) >= 2 then
    perform private.post_journal(
      p_business_id, now(), 'Penjualan ' || v_invoice_number, 'penjualan', v_transaction_id, v_journal_lines
    );
  end if;
```

**void_transaction journal-reversal block** (lines 400–418):

```sql
  v_journal_lines := '[]'::jsonb;
  if v_tx.total > 0 then
    v_journal_lines := v_journal_lines || jsonb_build_array(
      jsonb_build_object('account_code', '4-001', 'debit', v_tx.subtotal + v_tx.service, 'credit', 0),
      jsonb_build_object('account_code', '1-001', 'debit', 0, 'credit', v_tx.total)
    );
    if v_tx.tax > 0 then
      v_journal_lines := v_journal_lines || jsonb_build_array(
        jsonb_build_object('account_code', '2-200', 'debit', v_tx.tax, 'credit', 0)
      );
    end if;
  end if;
  if v_tx.total_cost > 0 then
    v_journal_lines := v_journal_lines || jsonb_build_array(
      jsonb_build_object('account_code', '1-200', 'debit', v_tx.total_cost, 'credit', 0),
      jsonb_build_object('account_code', '5-001', 'debit', 0, 'credit', v_tx.total_cost)
    );
  end if;
  if jsonb_array_length(v_journal_lines) >= 2 then
    perform private.post_journal(
      p_business_id, now(), 'Void ' || v_tx.invoice_number, 'void', p_transaction_id, v_journal_lines
    );
  end if;
```

Note `void_transaction`'s header `select` was widened to pull the split fields it needs for reversal: `select t.id, t.voided, t.total, t.subtotal, t.service, t.tax, t.total_cost, t.invoice_number into v_tx ... for update;` (line 362). `v_journal_lines` is declared as `v_journal_lines jsonb;` in both functions' `declare` blocks.

**PPN/tax handling pattern** (this is the piece your memory flagged): PPN is **never** blended into the revenue credit. `1-001 Kas & Bank` is debited for the *full* `v_total` (subtotal + service + tax — what the customer actually paid), but the credit side is split: `4-001 Pendapatan Penjualan` only gets `subtotal + service`, and `2-200 PPN Keluaran (Utang Pajak)` gets `v_tax` as a separate liability credit line — only emitted `if v_tax > 0`. Void does the exact mirror: debit `4-001` for `subtotal+service`, debit `2-200` for `tax` (if any), credit `1-001` for the full `total`.

**HPP/Persediaan conditional pattern**: completely decoupled from the revenue lines via a second, independent `if v_total_cost > 0 then ... end if;` block that appends its own two lines (`5-001` debit / `1-200` credit) to the same `v_journal_lines` array. This was a deliberate fix (see `20260709120000_fix_zero_total_hpp_posting.sql`'s header comment) so that a 100%-discounted sale (`v_total = 0`, revenue lines skipped) still posts HPP/Persediaan if stock was consumed (`v_total_cost > 0`). The final `perform private.post_journal(...)` only fires `if jsonb_array_length(v_journal_lines) >= 2` (i.e., only if *something* accumulated — either revenue lines, cost lines, or both), avoiding calling `post_journal` with an empty/1-line array which would raise inside `post_journal` itself.

