## 5. Does `ticket_transactions`/`ticket_categories` support PPN/tax?

**Yes**, fully, mirroring fnb/retail's exact pattern. From the `ticket_transactions` table DDL (`20260706200000_ticket_venue.sql`, lines 102–124):

```sql
create table public.ticket_transactions (
  id uuid primary key default gen_random_uuid(),
  business_id uuid not null references public.businesses (id) on delete cascade,
  shift_id uuid references public.shifts (id) on delete set null,
  cashier_id uuid not null references public.cashiers (id),
  member_id uuid references public.members (id) on delete set null,
  invoice_number text not null,
  date timestamptz not null default now(),
  is_holiday boolean not null default false,
  subtotal numeric(12, 2) not null default 0,
  service numeric(12, 2) not null default 0,
  tax numeric(12, 2) not null default 0,
  total numeric(12, 2) not null default 0,
  payment_method text not null,
  received numeric(12, 2),
  change numeric(12, 2) not null default 0,
  voided boolean not null default false,
  voided_at timestamptz,
  void_reason text,
  voided_by uuid references public.cashiers (id),
  constraint ticket_transactions_business_id_invoice_number_key
    unique (business_id, invoice_number)
);
```

`subtotal`, `service`, `tax`, `total` columns exist, and inside `checkout_ticket_transaction` they're computed identically to `checkout_transaction`:

```sql
  if v_business.service_enabled then
    v_service := round(v_subtotal * v_business.service_rate / 100);
  end if;

  if v_business.tax_enabled then
    v_tax := round((v_subtotal + v_service) * v_business.tax_rate / 100);
  end if;

  v_total := v_subtotal + v_service + v_tax;
```

`v_business` is populated from `select b.tax_enabled, b.tax_rate, b.service_enabled, b.service_rate from public.businesses b` — the same `businesses` table columns fnb/retail uses, and the migration comment (line 6, `20260706200000_ticket_venue.sql`) explicitly says: *"Reuse cashiers/shifts/pengaturan pajak-service yang sudah ada di businesses — tidak ada konsep baru di sana"* ("Reuse the existing cashiers/shifts/tax-service settings on businesses — no new concept there"). So **you should mirror the exact same PPN-split pattern** as `checkout_transaction`/`void_transaction` §3 above: debit Kas & Bank for `v_total`, credit revenue account for `subtotal + service`, credit `2-200` for `tax` (conditionally, if `tax > 0`).

**`ticket_categories`** (lines 21–32) has no tax-related columns — tax/service is business-level, not per-category, same as fnb/retail.

