## Summary of what a new migration needs to do

1. Add a new `perform private.post_journal(...)` block inside `checkout_ticket_transaction`, right before `return query select v_transaction_id, v_invoice_number;` — gated on `v_total > 0` (or more precisely, whenever the 2-line array is non-empty), using `'penjualan'` as source (or a new `'tiket'` value if you extend the `journal_entries_source_check` constraint) and `v_transaction_id` as `source_id`.
2. Add the mirrored reversal block inside `void_ticket_transaction` — but first widen its header `select t.id, t.voided into v_tx ...` to also pull `t.total, t.subtotal, t.service, t.tax, t.invoice_number` (there's no `total_cost` to pull, unlike fnb/retail's void).
3. Decide whether to reuse `4-001 Pendapatan Penjualan` or add a new `4-002 Pendapatan Tiket` account to `seed_default_accounts` (currently no ticket-specific account exists; adding one means also backfilling existing `tiket`-type businesses the same way `20260710140000_ppn_liability.sql` and `20260710150000_fixed_assets_depreciation.sql` did with their `do $$ ... perform private.seed_default_accounts(b.id); ... $$` backfill blocks).
4. No HPP/Persediaan lines are needed or possible — tickets have zero cost-basis columns anywhere in the schema.

